<span data-as=3D"p">Importantly, LangGraph knows whether a particular step =
has been executed previously. If it has, LangGraph simply <em>re-plays</em>=
 that particular step in the graph and does not re-execute the step, but on=
ly for the steps <em>before</em> the provided <code>checkpoint_id</code>. A=
ll of the steps <em>after</em> <code>checkpoint_id</code> will be executed =
(i.e., a new fork), even if they have been executed previously. See this <a=
 class=3D"link" href=3D"https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langgraph/use=
-time-travel">how to guide on time-travel to learn more about replaying</a>=
.</span>
