4H184c-13.3 0-24-10.7-24-24s10.7-24 24-24z"></path></svg></div></a></div><s=
pan class=3D"cursor-pointer"><code>values</code></span></h4>
<span data-as=3D"p">These are the values that will be used to update the st=
ate. Note that this update is treated exactly as any update from a node is =
treated. This means that these values will be passed to the <a class=3D"lin=
k" href=3D"https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langgraph/graph-api#reduce=
rs">reducer</a> functions, if they are defined for some of the channels in =
the graph state. This means that <a href=3D"https://reference.langchain.com=
/python/langgraph/graphs/#langgraph.graph.state.CompiledStateGraph.update_s=
tate" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noreferrer" class=3D"link"><code>update_stat=
e</code></a> does NOT automatically overwrite the channel values for every =
channel, but only for the channels without reducers. Let=E2=80=99s walk thr=
ough an example.</span>
